  "build_note": {
    "pattern": "One extraction call per packet with strict JSON and a closed exception vocabulary. The administrator record sits in the prompt so the model can compare commitment, KYC, and custodian. A second call turns the extraction into an internal checklist. A third drafts the LP status note for two packets. All three are parsed defensively.",
    "eval": "65 checks: 60 field cells across five packets, plus 5 exception sets. An exception set passes only when the kind and every severity match. Exact match after normalising money, dates, and yes/no values. In-sample, so it describes these five documents, not the next one.",
    "limits": [
      "Text intake only. No PDF parsing, OCR, or document storage.",
      "No Allocate API, custodian API, e-signature, wire, or filing integration.",
      "No model output is sent to an LP. The status note waits for a named approval.",
      "The exception log is a synthetic administrator record, not a real NIGO feed."
    ]
  }
